### CAMPAIGNS API
### ==========================================

### 3. Create a Campaign (Use the ID from step 1 for google_sheet_id)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/campaigns HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "campaign_name": "PARIPEX September Batch 2",
  "google_sheet_id": 1,
  "scheduled_at": "2026-09-02 16:00:00",
  "rate_limit_per_minute": 10
}

### 4. Get All Campaigns
GET http://localhost:3000/api/campaigns HTTP/1.1

### Create a New Campaign (Batch 2)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/campaigns HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "campaign_name": "PARIPEX September Batch 3 (Test Unsubscribe) with proper unsubscribe link",
  "google_sheet_id": 1,
  "scheduled_at": "2026-09-02 17:00:00",
  "rate_limit_per_minute": 10
}
### Create Campaign with Specific Sender
POST http://localhost:3000/api/campaigns HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "campaign_name": "PARIPEX Batch from Editor A",
  "google_sheet_id": 1,
  "sender_email": "editor.a@worldwidejournals.co.in",
  "scheduled_at": "2026-09-03 10:00:00",
  "rate_limit_per_minute": 10
}